      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "A nonzero gcd yields both exact natural cofactors and their constructive coprimality."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0005.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0005",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 0,
      "name": "crt_gcd_lcm_distributes_scaled_coprime",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1027,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Factoring a common gcd scale reduces unrestricted gcd--LCM distributivity to genuinely coprime cofactors."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0006.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0006",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 2,
      "name": "crt_gcd_lcm_distributes_nonzero",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1028,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "GCD distributes over the actual binary LCM for a nonzero left input and nonzero comparison input; the right input may be zero."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0007.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0007",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 0,
      "name": "crt_gcd_lcm_distributes_zero_left",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1029,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "The zero-left-modulus boundary of gcd--LCM distributivity follows from exact divisibility, not a positivity assumption."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0008.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0008",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 1,
      "name": "crt_gcd_lcm_distributes_zero_comparison",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1030,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Comparison with zero turns all three gcds into their other inputs and preserves the exact original LCM."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0009.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0009",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 3,
      "name": "crt_gcd_lcm_distributes",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1031,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Unconditional constructive gcd(lcm(a,b),n)=lcm(gcd(a,n),gcd(b,n)), including every zero boundary."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC000A.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC000A",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 0,
      "name": "crt_prefix_gcd_congruences_drop_last",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1032,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Pointwise congruence modulo decoded gcds restricts to the preceding finite prefix."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC000B.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC000B",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 4,
      "name": "crt_prefix_gcd_congruences_lcm",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1033,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Induction over every finite decoded modulus list lifts pointwise gcd congruences to congruence modulo the gcd of its exact list LCM; zero moduli and the empty list are included."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC000C.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC000C",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 0,
      "name": "crt_pairwise_compatible_prefix_induces_gcd_congruences",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1034,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Pairwise compatibility and an actual prefix solution imply every gcd congruence needed for the next merge, without any dominating-last or coprimality assumption."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC000D.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC000D",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 5,
      "name": "crt_pairwise_compatible_prefix_implies_merge_compatible",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1035,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Every pairwise gcd-compatible finite list satisfies every actual predecessor-LCM merge condition, including arbitrary noncoprime and zero moduli."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC000E.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC000E",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 6,
      "name": "crt_pairwise_compatible_prefix_solution_exists",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1036,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Unrestricted finite-list generalized CRT: every pairwise-compatible decoded residue/modulus list has a genuine simultaneous natural solution, including zero and repeated moduli and empty lists."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC000F.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC000F",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 6,
      "name": "crt_pairwise_compatible_prefix_canonical_exists_unique",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1037,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Full constructive canonical generalized CRT for arbitrary finite pairwise-compatible positive moduli: an exact list LCM and a unique strictly bounded simultaneous solution, with no supplied merge invariant or dominating modulus."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0010.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0010",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 0,
      "name": "crt_canonical_prefix_solution_implies_normalized",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1038,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Every historical strictly bounded canonical solution is also a zero-safe normalized solution, without changing either definition."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0011.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0011",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 0,
      "name": "crt_normalized_prefix_solution_unique",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1039,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Normalized representatives are literally unique at every list LCM; the zero case uses congruence equality, not a false bound below zero."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0012.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0012",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 1,
      "name": "crt_prefix_solution_normalized_exists",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1040,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Every simultaneous solution has a normalized representative for its exact list LCM, with zero retained rather than divided by."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0013.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0013",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 7,
      "name": "crt_pairwise_compatible_prefix_normalized_exists_unique",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1041,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Full zero-inclusive generalized CRT: every arbitrary pairwise-compatible finite list has its exact LCM and a unique normalized simultaneous solution; neither positivity nor an operational merge invariant is assumed."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0014.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0014",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 7,
      "name": "crt_pairwise_compatible_prefix_solvable_iff",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1042,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Exact pairwise gcd compatibility is necessary and sufficient for solvability of every finite natural congruence list, including zero moduli."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0015.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0015",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 6,
      "name": "crt_pairwise_compatible_prefix_merge_iff",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1043,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "Pairwise compatibility and the formerly stronger predecessor-LCM merge invariant are constructively equivalent for arbitrary finite natural lists."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0016.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0016",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 0,
      "name": "crt_normalized_prefix_solution_class_iff_lcm",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1044,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "All simultaneous solutions form exactly the congruence class of the normalized solution modulo the exact list LCM, also when that LCM is zero."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0017.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0017",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
      "kind": "theorem",
      "layer": 0,
      "name": "crt_normalized_zero_lcm_all_solutions_unique",
      "proof_bundle_node_id": 1045,
      "scope": "candidate",
      "stable_member": false,
      "summary": "At zero list LCM every actual simultaneous solution equals the normalized one; no bound or normalization premise is imposed on the comparison solution."
    },
    {
      "alpha_checked_use": true,
      "alpha_edition_version": "v29",
      "alpha_first_enrolled_version": "v27",
      "href": "tag/FC0018.html?v=2db42c10aa31",
      "id": "FC0018",
      "independent_lean_bundle_verified": true,
